LAYER 6: THERMAL GRADIENT AND CLOCK STABILITY\uc0\u8232 Clock speed fluctuations (Throttling) introduce timing jitter into the execution stream.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. GOVERNOR LOCKING\
ADA sets the Scaling Governor to "performance" and the Energy Performance Preference (EPP) to "0" (Maximum Performance).\
THERMAL STRATEGY: ADA locks the clock to the highest stable frequency to prevent thermal-induced downclocking, ensuring that T_cycle remains constant throughout the entire execution period.\
